{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified VAI 840 days before the shortage posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D6"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Fludarabine phosphate is not on FDA's current shortage list as of 2026-10-21; FDA's history shows an earlier shortage first posted on 2022-05-06, since resolved.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspection 1142104 at NerPharMa S.r.l. ended 2020-01-17 and was classified VAI, with the classification letter dated 2021-05-19 — 840 days before FDA posted the shortage on 2022-05-06.",
      "cites": ["D6", "E10"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product label for NDC 45963060955 names ACTAVIS TOTOWA as the manufacturing plant.",
      "cites": ["E6"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A separate label for NDC 59923060402 names NerPharMa SRL (FEI 3004762406) as a registered manufacturing plant with a VAI inspection on 2024-09-13.",
      "cites": ["E12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East holds 15 vials of the 50 mg/2 mL presentation at 3.4 vials per day, giving 4.4 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale General holds 82 vials of the same presentation at 4.5 vials per day, giving 18.2 days on hand.",
      "cites": ["D4"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The recommended action is to transfer 18 vials of 50 mg/2 mL, 2 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would leave Corvale General with 14 days and bring Corvale East to 10 days.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    }
  ]
}
